@0    = ~T-toi ?~
@1    = ~Incroyable ! Tu me reconnais après toutes ces années ! Ta conscience a repris le dessus au fil des ans ?~
@2    = ~M-mais tu es morte !~
@3    = ~Morte ? Oh non, pas morte mais presque. Grâce à toi et à tes amis, vous m'avez laissé pour morte, sous une pile de cadavres. Après plusieurs jours dans cette situation, tu ne peux pas imaginer combien l'esprit d'une personne peut en être affecté.~
@4    = ~En parlant de tes amis, où sont-ils ?~
@5    = ~Où..où sont-ils ? Je ne sais pas.~
@6    = ~Allons, Valis, je pense que tu sais au moins où est Cormak. Vous deux étiez les meilleurs amis après tout. Maintenant parles et je te libère.~
@7    = ~(Valis réfléchit brièvement puis répond.) Cormak ce trouve dans la forêts des collines d'Umar. Il dirige un groupe de bandits dans le coin.~
@8    = ~Merci mon joli, je suis sûr que c'était difficile pour toi de trahir ton ami. Maintenant meurs.~
@9    = ~M-mais tu disais que tu allais me libérer !~
@10   = ~Oh mais, c'est ce que je vais faire ! Ne bouge pas, ça ne fera mal qu'un instant.~
@11   = ~Va au diable, je ne tomberai pas sans combattre !~
@12   = ~Hé vous ! La bourse ou la vie. Attendez, tout bien réfléchis, on va prendre les deux ! Ha ha !~
@13   = ~Toujours aussi cinglé après tout ce temps, je vois.~
@14   = ~Eh ? Par l'enfer, qui êtes-vous ?~
@15   = ~Callisto T'sarran, mais je doute que tu te souviennes de moi. Après tout, tes méfaits à mon égard remontent à bien des années.~
@16   = ~Je me rappelle de ce nom. C’était celui d'une catin elfe qui dévastait villes et villages abritant ses soi-disant « ennemis », mais je n'ai plus entendu parler de cette folle depuis bien longtemps.~
@17   = ~What crimes did I do against you?~
@18   = ~Remember the elven village named Sylla'cerra?~
@19   = ~Ah yes an event from my young and crazy days. That was a village that didn't pay us tribute, so we razed it to the ground and butchered its people to make an example out of. What you call a crime, I call a days work. I gather you are one of those rare survivors who is seeking revenge?~
@20   = ~(Callisto glares at him, her hatred clearly evident towards Cormak.)~
@21   = ~I see we made a mistake, one that needs to be corrected. There were no survivors at that village, men attack!~
@22   = ~Hey watch where you are going!~
@23   = ~(Callisto eyes widen.) YOU!~
@24   = ~Yes? Do I know you? Hmm. You are a fine looking woman, one that I would have remembered if I had met you.~
@25   = ~Y-you're the one who killed my sister! Beheaded her! Traitor to your kind by associating with the drow!~
@26   = ~Ah my younger days have caught up with me it seems. This must be about that backwater village we plundered, that is the only time that I was associated with the drow.~
@27   = ~A lot of death occurred that day I seem to recall. It gave me practice in honing my killing abilities to become the great assassin that I am now. You should leave before you anger me.~
@28   = ~You admit to your crimes freely? Your death shall be slow and painful!~
@29   = ~Foolish action you're taking female. You will die this day. But before you die, know this; I did get a good laugh when I beheaded that young harlot. Seeing her blood splatter on your face, the look of horror and surprise on your face, it amused me so. Too bad that filthy blood of hers stained my good shirt.~
@30   = ~By the way, how are your ears doing? I don't see them sticking out like your typical elven ears do. Our ears, a source of pride and the one distinction that separates us from lowly races like humans. You could pass off as *human*. (Marius spits on the ground.)~
@31   = ~You bastard! You and your drow masters killed my village, killed my family, mutilated and scarred me! I have suffered greatly, endured and became stronger for it!~ ~Come on! I'm going to give you some suffering before you die! The last, the very last thing you will see is my smiling face as your life leaves your body!~ [call19]
@32   = ~So be it! This will be quick and sweet!~
@33   = ~Ah what is this? I see a surface elf has made her way down here and she looks familiar. Hmmm, yes very familiar. Do you recall her, Aliska?~
@34   = ~She bares the resemblance of an elven woman who's skull I crushed years ago. It would appear that the daughter has found us finally, ready to exact her revenge! Hello, Callisto.~
@35   = ~(Callisto says nothing, this surprise has left her speechless.)~
@36   = ~Surprised our "child"? We certainly do remember our creation and have kept track of her progress.~
@37   = ~W-what do you mean by "your creation"?~
@38   = ~It was a bet I made with Nastor. I bet him I could turn a surface elf into a drow. Not in appearance mind you, but in the heart, the mind, and the fiery passion that makes us drow. So I succeeded and won that bet.~
@39   = ~That you did my dear Aliska. I never should have doubt your abilities to make a surface elf like one of us. Can't you feel the hatred and the look of revenge coming from her?~
@40   = ~Oh that I can Nastor, that I can. So Callisto we made you is what it boils down to. We kept track of your exploits, your savage attacks on those who did you wrong. We even allowed you to "find" us here.~
@41   = ~Well, to tell the truth, you are not the first creation. Those elves and humans that helped in the raid were the results of my manipulation.~
@42   = ~My sister is quite good at turning others into blood seeking savages.~
@43   = ~Indeed. It's amazing how much pain one can endure, but in the end, the mind will surrender. Once that happens, they become our play things who will do what they are told.~
@44   = ~You butchered my family, my village over some sick bet?~
@45   = ~Why yes but I didn't expect you to live. Even when I heard you lived, I expected you to turn into some weakling who whined and cried about their unfortunate past and the transgressions waged against her. Imagine my surprise when I saw you rise above that and became like us. Aliska was a genius to see the fire in you and chose you in our bet.~
@46   = ~Come now Nastor, you make me blush.~
@47   = ~He speaks the truth my dear, Aliska. What you did with this surface elf far exceeds what I did.~
@48   = ~ENOUGH! You dare compare me to the likes of you! I'll show you your beating heart before you die!~
@49   = ~You really need to think this over, Callisto. Confrontation with your betters would be a miscalculation on your part. I thought you were smarter than this.~
@50   = ~After all we made you, we can destroy you.~
@51   = ~We allowed you to live so you can wreak fury upon the surface world. Why should we destroy the foul surfacers when we can have someone else do it for us? We will grant you safe passage to the surface world to continue your destruction. Ah yes, our very own destroyer on the surface world causing havoc!~
@52   = ~I don't think she's going to do what we wish any more. Look into her eyes!~
@53   = ~Aiieeee!!~ [call11]
@54   = ~Oh my, she's turning on us, Aliska, it would appear you lost the bet after all.~
@55   = ~How unfortunate and such a waste of talent. Guards, destroy this surface trash and her companions!~
@56   = ~By the gods not you!~
@57   = ~Soran, my little betraying captain! So nice to see you again! I was hoping to meet up with you and what is left of my rag tag mob.~
@58   = ~We don't want any trouble, Callisto. We just want to be left alone in peace.~
@59   = ~Peace is what you seek? Oh I will give you peace, Soran, not a problem.~
@60   = ~Glad to hear it. You and your friends can leave and we will go our separate ways.~
@61   = ~Not so fast, Soran. I haven't given you your peace yet. (The hatred in Callisto's eyes betrays her intentions.)~
@62   = ~To arms men! She means to attack!~
